            <ArticleTitle>The roentgenographic and clinical findings in Whipple's disease. A review of 8 patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>268-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Out of 8 patients with Whipple's disease, 7 had roentgenographic findings consisting of slight dilatation of the small bowel, with thickening of the mucosal folds. The eighth patient had no abnormality on roentgenographic study. This series represents the first in which the roentgenographic changes have been quantitatively assessed. Confirmation of the diagnosis by biopsy is important because antibiotic treatment results in marked improvement both clinically and roentgenographically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
